  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA-2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image-only, singleprofile, ResNet50) achieves only 20.8%, establishing RNA as the stronger modality and single-profile PCA as our current best baseline. Uncertainty: We have no data on whether multiprofile aggregation improves RNA performance, yet multiprofile is a prerequisite for all multimodal multiprofile configurations (configs 018–051). Question tested: config_002 is a minimal, single-variable extension of config_001 (singleprofile → multiprofile + avgpool, same PCA-2000 encoder), isolating the effect of multi-profile aggregation. Why best next step: With only 2 experiments completed, reducing uncertainty about whether multiprofile helps is critical because it gates the viability of the entire multimodal-multiprofile branch (24 of 51 remaining configs). If avgpool aggregation lifts accuracy meaningfully over 48.5%, it validates the multiprofile pipeline and justifies investing further in transformer aggregation and multimodal fusion. If it does not help, we avoid wasting budget on multiprofile variants and can focus on encoder improvements or single-profile multimodal fusion instead."
}

